CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ specialization: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ its bound: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ primary: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ static storage duration: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
already declared with different type
--
An explicit specialization of a variable template got the flags of a local
variable (its declaring scope is the template scope of `template <>'), so
it was never initialized; and the implicit instantiation of the primary
template for the same arguments, with an array of unknown bound, was
rejected as a conflicting redeclaration.  The MSVC STL's from_chars
(__DIGIT_TABLE) failed on VS 2022.
